{"nodes": [{"id": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_protocol_stage_protocol", "label": "Stage Protocol (runtime execution behaviour)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": ".claude/aidlc-common/protocols/stage-protocol.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One protocol referenced by every stage file, covering behaviour (gates, question flow, state tracking) while stage-definition.md covers file format \u2014 the two concerns are split so a stage author reads format and a stage runner reads behaviour."}, {"id": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_protocol_voice_contract", "label": "Voice contract (narrate the work, not the plumbing)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".claude/aidlc-common/protocols/stage-protocol.md", "source_location": "### Talking to the user (the voice contract)", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The user is a developer shipping their own project who never asked to learn the framework's internals, so a reserved internal vocabulary (engine, directive, dispatch, conductor, harness, scope grid, swarm, entropy, the ARS component names) is barred from chat narration. The rule governs words only and changes no step, tool call, audit event, or gate semantic."}, {"id": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_protocol_approval_gates", "label": "Approval gates (HARD STOP, no emergent behavior)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/aidlc-common/protocols/stage-protocol.md", "source_location": "## 1. Approval Gates", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The gate is a non-negotiable hard stop with a fixed option order (Approve first, Request Changes second), and the held gate is recorded before the human answers it, so the workflow cannot drift past a decision the human never made."}, {"id": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_protocol_question_format", "label": "Question format and tri-mode question flow", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/aidlc-common/protocols/stage-protocol.md", "source_location": "## 3. Question Format", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Guided, self-guided, and chat modes all converge on the same questions file, so the file stays the single source of truth regardless of how the human chose to answer; contradiction detection and overconfidence prevention are mandatory so ambiguity is resolved inside the stage rather than carried forward."}, {"id": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_protocol_reviewer_invocation", "label": "Reviewer invocation (12a): adversarial and advisory review classes", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".claude/aidlc-common/protocols/stage-protocol.md", "source_location": "## 12a. Reviewer Invocation", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Adversarial is the default where findings are machine-checkable and fix loops converge (Construction); advisory is the default for human-gated prose stages where readiness is a judgment call that belongs to the human at the gate. The reviewer never blocks the workflow and never sees the builder's plan or diary, so its judgment is independent while the human keeps final say. On a NOT-READY the LEAD alone is re-invoked, not the whole ensemble, because review findings are artifact defects and the lead owns the artifacts."}, {"id": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_protocol_review_freeze", "label": "Terminal review receipt and review freeze", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".claude/aidlc-common/protocols/stage-protocol.md", "source_location": "## 12a, step 3", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Once a terminal receipt is recorded, writing to a produces[] artifact invalidates it and the engine refuses the gate, so a reviewed artifact cannot be quietly edited after review. Riding suggestions are quoted verbatim for the human instead of applied, since a suggestion was explicitly not grounds for NOT-READY and therefore is not grounds for editing past the receipt either. The precondition is hard on the review having happened and soft on its verdict."}, {"id": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_protocol_reviewer_dispatch_record", "label": "Reviewer dispatch record (.aidlc-reviewer-dispatch.json)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/aidlc-common/protocols/stage-protocol.md", "source_location": "## 12a, Dispatch record", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The record is where the spot-check carve-out is granted and is what lets a PreToolUse hook enforce the reviewer read-scope bound deterministically instead of trusting prose; it is deleted after the review because a leftover record would keep refusing sibling access for later unrelated work."}, {"id": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_protocol_learnings_ritual", "label": "Learnings ritual (13): tool-as-actor learning loop", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".claude/aidlc-common/protocols/stage-protocol.md", "source_location": "## 13. Learnings Ritual", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Detection, surfacing, routing, and writing are deterministic while judgment stays the user's, so learnings cannot be invented by the model. Stage files are immutable framework artefacts and the harness is the mutable surface, with one carve-out for the sensors: import list; a confirmed learning lands in the same method files the resolver already reads, so there is no parallel learnings tier and no widen-to-org path."}, {"id": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_protocol_depth_guidance", "label": "Depth guidance and scope-to-depth mapping", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/aidlc-common/protocols/stage-protocol.md", "source_location": "## 8. Depth Guidance", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_protocol_test_strategy", "label": "Test Strategy levels (minimal / standard / comprehensive)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/aidlc-common/protocols/stage-protocol.md", "source_location": "### Test Strategy", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Test volume is a declared strategy level carried in state rather than a per-stage guess, so the amount of testing scales with the work instead of being reinvented each stage."}, {"id": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_protocol_subagent_return_summary", "label": "Subagent return summary and contribution file format (11)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/aidlc-common/protocols/stage-protocol.md", "source_location": "## 11. Subagent Return Summary", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A fixed return shape with an identity-marker first line lets the audit trail record which agent actually ran, and the context-budget rule passes paths rather than file bodies because subagents cannot see conversation history and would otherwise be handed unbounded context."}, {"id": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_protocol_audit_log", "label": "Append-only per-clone audit shards", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".claude/aidlc-common/protocols/stage-protocol.md", "source_location": "## 4. State Tracking", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "State fields, checkboxes, and audit rows are tool-owned silent bookkeeping writes rather than narrated prose, so lifecycle transitions cannot be faked in conversation; the trail is per-clone sharded and append-only, which makes it the canonical source of what happened."}], "edges": [{"source": "_claude_agents_aidlc_architecture_reviewer_agent_architecture_reviewer", "target": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_protocol_reviewer_invocation", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".claude/aidlc-common/protocols/stage-protocol.md", "source_location": "## 12a, step 2", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "_claude_agents_aidlc_product_lead_agent_advisory_dispatch", "target": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_protocol_reviewer_invocation", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".claude/aidlc-common/protocols/stage-protocol.md", "source_location": "## 12a, review_class advisory", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "_claude_agents_aidlc_architecture_reviewer_agent_adversarial_posture", "target": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_protocol_reviewer_invocation", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".claude/aidlc-common/protocols/stage-protocol.md", "source_location": "## 12a, adversarial review contract", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "_claude_agents_aidlc_architecture_reviewer_agent_reviewer_read_scope", "target": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_protocol_reviewer_dispatch_record", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".claude/aidlc-common/protocols/stage-protocol.md", "source_location": "## 12a, Dispatch record", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_protocol_stage_protocol", "target": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_protocol_voice_contract", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".claude/aidlc-common/protocols/stage-protocol.md", "source_location": "### Talking to the user", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_protocol_stage_protocol", "target": "_claude_aidlc_common_protocols_stage_protocol_approval_gates", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRA